    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSome homes simply offer more. More space, more style and more flexibility for modern family living. Extending to almost 2,000 sq.ft. over three beautifully designed floors, No. 34 Avonvale Manor combines contemporary luxury with uninterrupted countryside views, all just minutes from the heart of Wicklow Town.\n\nThis impressive home perfectly combines striking contemporary design, generous family accommodation and outstanding energy efficiency. Occupying an enviable position within this popular development, the property enjoys uninterrupted countryside views to the front while remaining just minutes from Wicklow Town's vibrant Main Street, excellent schools, supermarkets, sporting facilities and commuter transport links.\n\nDesigned with modern family living at its heart, the accommodation is both beautifully presented and exceptionally practical. Large windows flood the home with natural light, while the thoughtful layout offers an ideal balance between generous open-plan living spaces and well proportioned bedrooms and bathrooms.\n\nThe heart of the home is the magnificent open-plan kitchen, dining and family room, featuring an extensive range of contemporary fitted units, quartz worktops and a substantial central island that naturally becomes the focal point for everyday family life. Sliding doors open directly onto the rear garden, creating a seamless connection between indoor and outdoor living.\n\nArranged over three floors, the accommodation offers exceptional flexibility for modern families. Whether you require additional bedrooms, guest accommodation, dedicated home-working space or simply room to grow, the layout effortlessly adapts to changing lifestyles. The impressive principal suite occupying the upper floor provides a peaceful sanctuary away from the main living accommodation.\n\nOutside, generous off-street parking is provided to the front, while the enclosed rear garden offers a private space for entertaining, family enjoyment or relaxing in the evening sun. To the front, uninterrupted countryside views provide a wonderful sense of openness, a rare feature so close to the centre of Wicklow Town.\n\nAvonvale Manor is a wonderful low density development, offering the perfect balance of town convenience and coastal living. Wicklow Harbour, the Murrough, local beaches, schools, cafés, restaurants and excellent transport links are all within easy reach, while Dublin remains an easy commute via the N11/M11 and regular rail services.\n\nBeautifully finished throughout and presented in true walk-in condition, No. 34 Avonvale Manor represents an outstanding opportunity to acquire a substantial contemporary family home in one of Wicklow Town's most desirable addresses."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 6.01m x 2.60m\nWith high quality laminate flooring, guest wc and carpeted stairs to upper levels\n\nWC - 2.33m x 1.48m\nFully tiled guest wc with toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nLiving Room - 5.07m x 3.67m\nWell proportioned and bright with a large picture window the room boasts high quality laminate flooring and a wall mounted feature fire.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 5.39m x 5.73m\nTruly an impressive kitchen with bespoke cabinetry, intregrated appliances, large centre island and porcelian tiling throughout. Double doors lead to the patio and garden beyond.\n\nUtility Room - 1.53m x 3.03m\nGenerous utility with ample storage and counter space, plumbed for a washing machine and tiled floor.\n\nLanding - 5.90m x 1.93m\nCarpeted with storage\n\nStorage - 1.62m x 1.93m\n\n\nBedroom 1 - 8.62m x 4.74m\nPrimary suite on the uppermost level with generous room proportions, views to the countryside, built in storage and a large ensuite.\n\nEn-suite - 3.47m x 1.71m\nWith modern grey tiling, walk in shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nStorage - 1.62m x 1.88m\n\n\nLanding - 5.31m x 3.69m\n\n\nBedroom 2 - 5.07m x 3.69m\nPositioned to the front with views to the countryside, large picture window and built in wardrobes.\n\nEn-suite - 1.45m x 1.93m\nFully tiled ensuite with stylish grey tiles, walk in shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.45m x 3.16m\nDouble bedroom with views to the rear garden, carpet flooring and fitted wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 4 - 1.12m x 2.55m\nLarge fourth bedroom with garden views currently used as the home office.\n\nBathroom - 2.96m x 2.08m\nFamily bathroom with stylish grey tiling, bath, walk in shower, wc and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
